    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table, keeping each piece of logic where it belongs:\n\n1. **`model/Locality.java`** \u2014 the home of the pinned locality reference data. Added the `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneForRegion(String region)` lookup that returns the IANA name, or `null` when the region isn't in the table (e.g. `UNKNOWN`). This sits alongside the existing region/postcode tables so all locality reference data stays in one place.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `timezone(Owner owner)` mapping method that reuses the existing `locality(owner)` (the region from the customer code) and feeds it to `Locality.timezoneForRegion`, plus the `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` wiring. No duplication of the table.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `timezone` field to the Owner schema (read-only string) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
